{
  "requirement": "The harness MUST construct each assessment's mandatory input set by combining\nthe contributions specified by the requirements applicable to that subject and\nits inputs. A requirement that contributes inputs MUST cite this requirement and\ndefine which sources it contributes and when. The harness MUST include every\napplicable contribution, deduplicate identical selections, and report\nunresolvable mandatory inputs before inference. The complete set MUST be supplied\nin the initial model request.\nGenerated output under project-root `evidence/`, including symlink aliases, MUST\nbe omitted from mandatory inputs when the default exclusion applies. An explicit\nworkspace allow MUST permit those selections; an explicit disallow MUST abort\nunder {cite}`requirements.authoring.read_denial.mandatory`.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The reviewed tests adequately check `requirements.authoring.mandatory_inputs`. Each obligation maps to at least one test with assertions that would fail on a violation.\n\n**Combining every applicable contribution.**\n- `bundle_combines_direct_references_terms_and_current_existing_selectors` checks the combined set for a subject.\n  - It includes the subject declaration, the directly cited `requirements.base`, and the example `requirements.case`.\n  - It excludes the non-adjacent `requirements.distant`.\n  - It includes the `{test}` node `fn[test_ready]` and excludes the `{impl}` node and the parent `impl[Thing]`.\n  - It includes exactly two definitions.\n  - It checks that earlier-evidence inputs and judgments are not carried forward.\n  - For the example subject, it asserts the exact first input, including its text.\n- `only_edges_leaving_the_subject_contribute_inputs` checks which edges contribute.\n  - It covers the subject-to-cited, example-to-subject and parent-requirement directions.\n  - It covers `{impl}`, `{test}` and `{cite}` sites.\n- `anchored_files_contribute_root_node_inputs` asserts the exact input list for `:impl:` and `:test:` anchors.\n- `test_anchors_supply_only_the_selected_node` checks node-level anchors and checks the prompt.\n- `references_contribute_their_owning_outline_nodes` covers markdown sections, plain-text files and `{fixme}` metadata.\n- `citation_reviews_use_their_prompt_and_record_the_item_and_citations` and `site_reviews_use_their_prompt_and_record_applies_and_the_site` cover the citation and site subject kinds.\n- `earlier_evidence_inputs_and_judgments_are_not_carried_forward` and `unresolvable_earlier_inputs_do_not_block_reassessment` check that earlier-evidence inputs are not carried forward and that stale ones do not block a new assessment.\n\n**Deduplication.**\n- `citation_review_inputs_combine_item_declarations_terms_and_built_ins_once` uses repeated cites, a shared term and a duplicated built-in. It asserts each appears exactly once and that there are five inputs in total.\n- `anchored_files_contribute_root_node_inputs` anchors the same file with both `:impl:` and `:test:`. The exact-equality assertion shows it appears once.\n\n**Unresolvable inputs reported before inference.**\n- `disallowed_mandatory_inputs_abort_preparation` and `unreadable_or_denied_anchors_fail_before_inference` check that preparation fails and that the error names the path.\n- `mandatory_inputs_outside_the_project_still_abort` covers an anchor outside the project.\n- `mandatory_git_inputs_require_staging_declarations_sources_and_terms` covers unstaged declarations and terms.\n- `unresolvable_mandatory_inputs_fail_before_any_model_request` in `tests/authoring_cli.rs` checks the end-to-end case. The CLI exits nonzero, the endpoint is never contacted, and the evidence file is unchanged.\n- The detail of the denial report, batch behaviour and usage record belongs to `requirements.authoring.read_denial.mandatory`, so it needs no test here.\n\n**Complete set in the initial request.**\n- The citation test asserts that the prompt contains the mandatory item's hash, the requirement text and the built-in text.\n- The site test asserts that the initial subject message equals the template filled with `model_mandatory_inputs`.\n- The CLI test `ollama_cli_delivers_sources_records_fixme_and_keeps_usage_content_free` checks that the first request carries the requirement, definition and test text. It also checks that implementation text is not delivered up front.\n- The redaction test checks the prompt built from the mandatory set.\n\n**Generated `evidence/` output.**\n- `generated_evidence_anchors_are_omitted_unless_allowed_and_abort_when_disallowed` covers all four cases.\n  - By default, an anchor into `evidence/` is omitted.\n  - By default, a symlink alias such as `alias/report.md` is omitted.\n  - An explicit allow includes the file.\n  - An explicit disallow aborts with `PermissionDenied` and names the path.\n- `generated_evidence_references_are_omitted_by_default` covers references discovered under `evidence/`, with and without an allow.\n\n**Obligation on other requirements to cite this one.** This is a book-structure obligation, and the book already carries many `{cite}` sites to this requirement. It is not a harness behavior, so it needs no test here.\n\nI found no accepted-violation scenario that the tests would miss.",
  "references": "5e119b23ee95abcacb9104190da269b67b7e85e7e3a806f9a712233a1e425674",
  "inputs": [
    {
      "requirements": "requirements.authoring.mandatory_inputs",
      "matches": [
        "requirements.authoring.mandatory_inputs"
      ],
      "text": [
        ":::{req} mandatory_inputs",
        "The harness MUST construct each assessment's mandatory input set by combining",
        "the contributions specified by the requirements applicable to that subject and",
        "its inputs. A requirement that contributes inputs MUST cite this requirement and",
        "define which sources it contributes and when. The harness MUST include every",
        "applicable contribution, deduplicate identical selections, and report",
        "unresolvable mandatory inputs before inference. The complete set MUST be supplied",
        "in the initial model request.",
        "Generated output under project-root `evidence/`, including symlink aliases, MUST",
        "be omitted from mandatory inputs when the default exclusion applies. An explicit",
        "workspace allow MUST permit those selections; an explicit disallow MUST abort",
        "under {cite}`requirements.authoring.read_denial.mandatory`.",
        ":::"
      ]
    },
    {
      "requirements": "requirements.authoring.read_denial.mandatory",
      "matches": [
        "requirements.authoring.read_denial.mandatory"
      ],
      "text": [
        ":::{req} read_denial.mandatory",
        "When source-access policy denies a mandatory input, the assessment MUST abort",
        "before any model request and report the denied path and reason to its caller;",
        "for an untracked file, the report MUST say what {cite}`requirements.authoring.read_denial.untracked`",
        "says. The aborted assessment MUST NOT write evidence or emit evidence JSON, and",
        "its usage record MUST identify the failure. In a batch, other assessments MUST",
        "continue, including queued assessments, and their successful writes MUST be",
        "retained; the command MUST return a nonzero exit status after the batch",
        "finishes.",
        ":::"
      ]
